      "content": "but that feels like a stretch. if Bruen says regulations have to be consistent with the historical tradition of the US, and most of those old laws weren't about preventing mass shootings or modern high-capacity mags, doesn't that basically mean any attempt at \"strict\" control is just going to get struck down? like, can you actually find a historical precedent for what people are trying to do now?",
