    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, but it feels like you're being a bit too diplomatic there. if the Court says you need a historical analogue and you can't find one for things like magazine limits or bans on certain types of rifles, isn't it just a massive legal failure to pretend those arguments are \"legitimate\"? at what point do we stop calling it a \"debate\" and just admit that the old way of thinking about gun control is basically dead in the eyes of the law?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
